WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.370
- Never even expected to
come down here and get stuck

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.470
down here as many years
as I have been down here.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.690
But it seems like it's open.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.160
Like you just do what you want to do.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.160
When I first got here, it was like, man,

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.300
I enjoy doing what I do,
getting high and stuff.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.703
Like when I came down here,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.760
it was like an open park.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.830
Like everywhere you go, they're
getting high in the streets

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:31.490
and sidewalks.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.573
Side of the buildings, at the parks.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.290
It seemed like the
police would just roll by

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.340
and it didn't really

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.083
bother them back then.

00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:43.080
So it's like I arrived,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:43.913
like I'm home now.

00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:45.363
I just get a high, like I want to.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:49.973
I forgot all about what life is about.

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.186
And

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.490
became a part of it.

00:01:00.874 --> 00:01:02.240
You know, what they call DTG, man.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.073
It's like,

00:01:12.702 --> 00:01:13.535
I've been through a whole lot

00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:14.513
and seen a whole lot.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.600
I've been stabbed four
times down here man.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:27.210
Seen people been thrown out
of windows of buildings.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:39.510
But I'm so adapted to the
life is like I gravitates.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.370
It's like magnetic to me.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.040
It's like wherever I do
decide to go leave it,

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.350
try to stay away.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.183
It's hard.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:57.570
I'm really glad I met so
many beautiful people.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:01.010
I've met a lot of people
that want to change.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:02.860
It's just don't know how like myself.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.460
I go to program and stay in
the program and I won't stay

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.973
because it don't seem like
that's where I want to be.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.960
Because there's nobody
there that I already know.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.573
- [Man] When you were a child.

00:02:23.573 --> 00:02:24.979
When you were young.

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:26.829
Did you have ambitions for your life?

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:28.650
- Yeah. I played sports.

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.300
I had played a lot of sports.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.723
I was good at sports.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.717
Baseball was really one
of my number one sports.

00:02:37.717 --> 00:02:39.323
And I played it pretty good.

00:02:40.642 --> 00:02:43.123
Why I had a scholarship
to go to New Mexico,

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:45.713
playing football.

00:02:45.713 --> 00:02:48.373
I was quarterback at Blair
High School in Pasadena.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.680
And as soon as I graduated high school,

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:55.030
I was already in the
gang-banging and hanging out

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.260
and ended up getting a
direct cell to the police

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.240
and they gave me eight years

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.840
and it messed my scholarship up.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.253
And

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.403
it's right there and it's like

00:03:11.403 --> 00:03:13.803
I didn't see fit to try
to do anything else that

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:18.180
had any other benefits besides

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:20.680
selling drugs,

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:21.513
getting high.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.383
Doing any other activities
that we do in the streets.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:32.580
Got being shot, you know

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:37.273
with a 12 gauge shotgun and
ended up in a coma for 76 days.

00:03:39.156 --> 00:03:39.989
- [Man] You?

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:40.822
- [Interviewee] Yeah.

00:03:40.822 --> 00:03:42.450
- [Man] When was this?

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.303
- [Interviewee] This was like,
when I was like 16 years old.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.010
I was gang banging heavily.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:57.083
And the guy walked in the
store and it was raining.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:01.980
And my coat was real wet

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.330
because I had been out
there all night already.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.440
So that's what kind of saved my life

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:12.550
because it didn't penetrate
all the way through

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.730
and it hit me right here
on my side right here

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.883
close to my chest.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.360
I still have buck shots in me.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.407
See my brothers and sisters
and siblings and stuff out.

00:04:31.757 --> 00:04:34.960
You know, they was
always in that lifestyle.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.530
And by me being the youngest, I liked it

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.450
what they was doing.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.900
And I wanted to be a part of,

00:04:40.545 --> 00:04:41.390
and my mom pulling me over here

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:44.100
telling me I needed to stay in school.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.713
You know, I did graduated high school.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.250
I wouldn't do nothing afterwards.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:56.380
I liked it to walk the streets

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.530
and hang on the streets
more than anything.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:06.620
I've been shot at seven
different times in my life.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.853
Stabbed three times.

00:05:09.456 --> 00:05:12.610
And hit by a bus, hit by Volkswagen.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:14.270
Bit by a dog.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.370
Through only trash can

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.960
Still weird, man.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.452
Just had a birthday.

00:05:33.452 --> 00:05:35.037
- [Man] How old are you now?

00:05:35.037 --> 00:05:35.870
- I'm 52.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.583
Yeah. I don't have any kids.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:48.307
Ain't nothing wrong with
me or nothing though.

00:05:48.307 --> 00:05:49.872
There's one young lady.

00:05:49.872 --> 00:05:50.860
I don't even know if
she had the baby or not.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:51.910
She said she was pregnant.

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:53.790
She left by the hotel.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.240
I don't even know where she at.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.630
I don't even know where she kept the baby.

00:05:57.630 --> 00:06:00.213
If she had the baby or
if she was pregnant.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.037
She told me she was pregnant.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:09.464
I have 76 nieces and nephews.

00:06:09.464 --> 00:06:10.297
- [Man] Wow.

00:06:10.297 --> 00:06:11.240
- That's pretty huge.

00:06:15.021 --> 00:06:17.568
I don't even know half of them.

00:06:17.568 --> 00:06:18.670
I don't even know half of them.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:19.820
- [Man] Sorry to bring your family.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.487
You grew up with one parent? Both parents?

00:06:23.487 --> 00:06:26.323
- Basically one, just my mom.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.283
My dad came around every periodically.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.061
All my brothers and sisters lived there

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:40.000
in that big house with my mom raised us.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.350
Doing everything she could.

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:43.740
My dad came in and out.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.590
I really didn't have too much
of a relationship with him.

00:06:49.313 --> 00:06:51.100
I kind of built up animosity towards him

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.963
because he would beat my mom
up all the time he come around.

00:06:56.518 --> 00:06:58.727
And so I really didn't too much

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:03.509
like to see him when he showed up.

00:07:03.509 --> 00:07:08.360
You know, my mom she was
almost like a caregiver.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.910
She just cared about everybody.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.630
A lot of my sisters

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.270
all my brothers and sisters
graduated high school.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.370
Couple of my brothers went to the service.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:23.681
I was more like the prodigal son.

00:07:23.681 --> 00:07:24.514
The only one, the prodigal son

00:07:24.514 --> 00:07:27.710
I just was like that knucklehead.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:28.860
Ended up in the streets

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:35.040
and first time I ever got shot
was like, I was 12 years old

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:42.710
and I was hanging out in the
park with a couple of friends.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:50.260
And I guess I wanted to
be a tough guy, a bold guy

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.360
and want to try to protect everybody else.

00:07:54.409 --> 00:07:55.340
And guy was like, man, I'll shoot you.

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:56.173
You know?

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.233
And I was like, I don't care.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:02.133
And he did.

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:04.743
What number, the 22.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.360
He shot me in my hand.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.290
Cause I put my hand up.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.123
But,

00:08:12.566 --> 00:08:14.710
and I thought I was
exempt after that, like,

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:15.640
you get shot by a gun.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:16.840
It didn't really matter.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.850
My mom always been a Christian lady

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:23.930
trying to raise up

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:27.887
raise her up to be spiritual,

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:31.863
to get to know who God is.

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.133
And

00:08:38.505 --> 00:08:41.030
I had a brother that would stay on me,

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:41.940
my older brother.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:44.290
And that was one of the reasons why

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.240
I played a lot of sports.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.913
Cause he was more like a dad.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.456
He stayed around with me and hung out

00:08:52.456 --> 00:08:55.243
with me and helped me with my
homework and school and stuff.

00:09:00.675 --> 00:09:04.175
And that was one of my strongest points is

00:09:06.530 --> 00:09:09.060
staying active with playing sports.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.023
I love sports.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.250
I would play the summertime.

00:09:12.250 --> 00:09:15.573
Play it, made it some leagues.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.703
Pop Warner Football.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.480
And I know it was hard for my
mom to pay for a lot of stuff

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:23.730
because she had 12 of us.

00:09:27.047 --> 00:09:30.030
And at the time they, you
know, they were part of the

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.113
lifestyle, you know.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.840
Pimps and you know,
what they call hookers.

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.130
I don't like to call women that.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:40.540
But my family, my sisters
and brothers was a part

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:42.840
of that lifestyle right there.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.723
And I thought that was a life to live.

00:09:45.569 --> 00:09:47.659
Cause they had a lot of money,

00:09:47.659 --> 00:09:48.509
in low rider cars

00:09:49.414 --> 00:09:50.247
and nice clothes

00:09:52.272 --> 00:09:54.020
and my mom was trying to get
me to see it the other way

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:55.750
but I couldn't see it
the other way because

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:59.800
I'm seeing this here visually
in my face and I ended

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:06.850
up selling drugs and that's how
I ended up going to the Penn

00:10:06.871 --> 00:10:07.704
for eight years.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.660
And I went to Folson Penitentiary

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:16.143
right after high school at the age of 18.

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:19.620
- [Man] You're a part
of a gang at that point?

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.370
- Yeah, I was a part of
Pasadena Raymond Crip.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:23.203
- [Man] Crips?

00:10:23.203 --> 00:10:27.783
- Yeah, I was real active in it.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.700
Back then, there really
wasn't a whole lot of shooting

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.750
back in the eighties and stuff.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.150
It's just a lot of fighting.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:41.973
We really didn't shoot too
much, but then I stepped out.

00:10:44.862 --> 00:10:46.029
I happened to,

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:48.347
I seen a...

00:11:05.755 --> 00:11:07.422
I had a best friend.

00:11:09.191 --> 00:11:11.191
He got shot in the head.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:26.793
I tried to hold his head.

00:11:27.911 --> 00:11:28.744
I tried to put...

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:41.863
I tried to put whatever
I could back inside.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.823
Had to hold it and shit.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:27.493
He was still talking to me
until he was like man...

00:12:28.633 --> 00:12:30.163
I tried to hold his flesh.

00:12:38.743 --> 00:12:39.576
I didn't care then after

00:12:39.576 --> 00:12:40.409
it was like, man

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.150
- That was my high school partner

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.740
in junior high and high school

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.210
and play sports together.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:56.130
And I always told myself,
I don't want to be

00:12:57.530 --> 00:13:00.270
that close to nobody else again because

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:02.120
to lose somebody that close it hurts.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:07.993
What ended up happening
was the closest one to me.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:13.760
He passes away you just like man,

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.023
so I stay down here.

00:13:22.445 --> 00:13:25.410
And I came down here and I
got introduced, downtown LA

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.363
and I came down here, man.

00:13:27.363 --> 00:13:29.260
I didn't come down here to stay though.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.243
And I came down here and I was shopping.

00:13:32.622 --> 00:13:33.703
I was in a relationship.

00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:40.221
The young lady that
worked for Twin Towers,

00:13:40.221 --> 00:13:41.250
she was a sheriff.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:43.740
She had twins and

00:13:47.123 --> 00:13:49.635
I came out here to go shopping
and I ended up downtown.

00:13:49.635 --> 00:13:52.830
I met this young lady and I
was getting high at the time.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.733
We'd go to the motel up there,

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.110
Cecil motel

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.005
to hang out and stuff.

00:14:01.005 --> 00:14:03.420
And she told me she'll be right back.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:07.630
And she left the door
cracked and some guys down

00:14:07.630 --> 00:14:11.193
that be down here, came in and robbed me.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:15.791
And I didn't have any more money

00:14:15.791 --> 00:14:18.063
and I don't know how to get home.

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.850
So I ended up staying down here.

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:24.703
I ended up robbing somebody else.

00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:27.610
And when I did that

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.060
I found where he was hanging all that,

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:32.200
getting high at

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.250
and ended up staying.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.560
And I walked around for two weeks.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.810
With the same clothes on.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.653
Didn't care about taking no shower.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:46.913
Didn't care about changing clothes.

00:14:49.957 --> 00:14:52.357
And people was telling
me, man get away from me.

00:14:55.928 --> 00:14:57.590
On God my feet was hurting.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.320
Sores, all on my foot.

00:15:08.247 --> 00:15:10.243
And I became a product of downtown.

00:15:11.780 --> 00:15:16.436
And almost every street
you could think of.

00:15:16.436 --> 00:15:17.686
I got high on.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.280
Man, I didn't seen some of the stuff.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.870
Some of the stuff happened downtown

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.970
that I'd never thought I'd see in my life.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:33.805
From the things that could make you smile,

00:15:33.805 --> 00:15:35.740
from the things that would make me cry.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.580
I never thought I'd see so much go on

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.130
in one little bitty small city.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:45.740
And the city has so
much clout like this is

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:51.053
this is the money city
with so much going on.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:57.500
I've been down here for so long.

00:15:57.500 --> 00:16:00.710
I hadn't got on GR for
like the first 10 years

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:01.780
I never got on GR

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.563
I was just hustling in the street.

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.013
Did not.

00:16:15.137 --> 00:16:17.313
I mean I was tired of all that.

00:16:19.595 --> 00:16:22.443
I would stay up so long,
like two, three, four days.

00:16:23.484 --> 00:16:27.990
And my body is so tired, but
I don't want to go lay down

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.253
to where I would fall on my face.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.590
I would literally try to
stay up and I couldn't and

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.520
my body would just give up

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:40.730
and give out on me and
I'll fall flat on my face

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:42.643
in the middle street or sidewalk.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.000
Bust my face open or bust my head

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:51.443
and still don't want
to go to the hospital.

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:53.840
Let me just stay there.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:10.913
I know I'm dealing with
a lot of pain, man.

00:17:16.463 --> 00:17:18.632
You know, I'm wanting
to get sober at times.

00:17:18.632 --> 00:17:19.760
Then it's times I don't...

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:25.040
sometimes I don't care

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:26.390
but majority of times I do.

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:30.019
- [Man] You ever been clean?

00:17:30.019 --> 00:17:32.493
- Yeah I cleaned up one
time, for like four years.

00:17:33.453 --> 00:17:35.880
And that was only because
I had got locked up

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:39.493
and they sent me to a program in Compton.

00:17:43.314 --> 00:17:45.040
It was called Quincy's Place.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:46.410
It was on Compton Boulevard

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.113
And I was going to meetings out there and

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.623
I met someone and she was real nice.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:56.443
She was a nurse.

00:17:56.443 --> 00:17:57.276
She was beautiful.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:02.320
And so she would always
say, just, don't go.

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:03.470
Just don't go downtown.

00:18:05.266 --> 00:18:08.100
And the whole time I was
sober, all I could think

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.350
about is my money to go
show them how I look.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.420
I want them to see how I'm looking now.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:20.270
And after like three and a half years,

00:18:20.270 --> 00:18:23.360
clean having some stuff,

00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:25.220
going to college.

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:27.144
I went to El Camino College

00:18:27.144 --> 00:18:31.260
I had picked up the degree

00:18:33.827 --> 00:18:34.660
in children's services.

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:37.553
I was got some education

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.040
And then I would just skip like three

00:18:42.934 --> 00:18:43.767
and a half years

00:18:45.707 --> 00:18:49.810
and I came downtown in a new car showing

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.933
them how I was doing.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:55.560
And after a month and a
half I was back at night.

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:08.581
- [Man] What's your grout?

00:19:08.581 --> 00:19:09.930
Is it-?

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:12.833
- Yeah, that's all I smoked,
it was crack cocaine.

00:19:14.270 --> 00:19:15.193
I'd try-

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.100
I can't even say I even tried other drugs

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:21.120
but I smoked it

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:26.350
just for the taste and
see the effect and then I

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.520
I tried Sharon.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.100
I will never ever try that again.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:30.933
It's...

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:32.703
wow

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:34.863
they scared me.

00:19:37.020 --> 00:19:38.230
That scared me.

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:41.163
You know, some embalming fluids and PCP.

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.420
They call it Sharon.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:47.900
And I tried that and
it's already bad enough

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:51.573
that it stinks so much, smells bad.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.083
And speed, crystal.

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:00.160
I don't even understand what
is the high, what's the rush.

00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:02.960
I don't even really understand
the feeling of that high.

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:05.410
They call it go fast.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:08.913
I mean. I see people
how they could stay up.

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:14.573
I see somebody stay up 21 days on speed.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:19.313
That's some daze.

00:20:21.095 --> 00:20:21.928
Wow.

00:20:27.578 --> 00:20:30.140
Well, all I smoke was crack cocaine.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:34.350
And I know I've had some
crack cocaine before to where

00:20:35.781 --> 00:20:37.810
feel like I was going into a heart attack.

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.560
I was about to have a heart attack.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.403
Or like I was going to go into a seizure.

00:20:45.210 --> 00:20:46.540
And it kind of made me want to stop

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:51.540
but then the craving be so intense

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:56.180
that monkey be on your back so heavily.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.803
To where it won't let you go.

00:21:00.740 --> 00:21:03.370
Just a month and a half ago, you know

00:21:04.645 --> 00:21:07.010
right outside right
here on Seventh and Stem

00:21:09.060 --> 00:21:11.613
two Spanish guys rolled up on me on bikes.

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:14.080
Two in the morning.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:17.453
With hoodies on

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.050
I don't even get a
chance to see their face.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.570
One riding on this side
and one riding on this side

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:26.360
and then coming in the
same way that I'm going.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:30.450
And I looked to my right to
see what this guy was gonna do.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:32.350
And this guy stabbed me in my stomach.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:37.340
Just recently he's just now healing.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.493
It's just a month ago.

00:21:42.120 --> 00:21:43.993
I was in ICU for six weeks.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:47.370
Couldn't use the bathroom.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:49.513
Couldn't pee.

00:21:52.069 --> 00:21:53.483
Couldn't defecate.

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:58.990
The worst pain I ran of my life.

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:00.533
- [Man] Did they rob you
or did they just stab you?

00:22:00.533 --> 00:22:02.660
- They stabbed me and they said

00:22:03.961 --> 00:22:05.110
(speaking in Spanish)

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:06.260
That means fuck niggas.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:10.650
And I thought it was like a joke.

00:22:10.650 --> 00:22:13.561
And then I went to try to
run, catch up with them.

00:22:13.561 --> 00:22:16.870
And I took like two steps
and I was out of breath.

00:22:16.870 --> 00:22:20.580
I bled for a long time
right here on this corner,

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:21.840
directly on the corner of the light.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:23.740
I walked to that corner and I sat down

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:26.533
and I was bleeding all over the place.

00:22:28.741 --> 00:22:33.190
And a guy rode up on his bike
and was like, man, smooth.

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:34.023
What's up, man?

00:22:35.483 --> 00:22:37.907
And I was like, my nigga I'm out.

00:22:37.907 --> 00:22:40.007
And he rode down here to the fire station.

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:46.664
Fire department, ambulance
came and picked me up.

00:22:46.664 --> 00:22:47.497
Well they he came and checked on me,

00:22:47.497 --> 00:22:49.077
and they called the ambulance

00:22:49.990 --> 00:22:54.990
and I was at USC medical for six weeks,

00:22:56.820 --> 00:22:57.770
barely can breathe.

00:22:59.200 --> 00:23:00.273
I was in a IV,

00:23:05.977 --> 00:23:07.427
I was in a breathing machine.

00:23:10.691 --> 00:23:12.891
And I didn't know if I
was going to make it.

00:23:28.887 --> 00:23:30.537
So I know I'm a living testimony.

00:23:33.253 --> 00:23:34.510
- [Man] Sorry?

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:36.273
- So I know I'm a living testimony.

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:40.450
I don't know what God's plans are for me.

00:23:43.540 --> 00:23:44.840
I know it got to be some good,

00:23:44.840 --> 00:23:47.427
but a lot of stuff be going
on way down sometimes.

00:23:51.440 --> 00:23:53.860
And still today, the guys can
walk by me and I wouldn't even

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:54.967
know who it was.

00:24:00.974 --> 00:24:02.531
Never even done that to him.

00:24:02.531 --> 00:24:04.680
I'm not even a racist person.

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:06.493
I'm a biased person, absolutely.

00:24:08.860 --> 00:24:10.170
I remember wake up in the morning,

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:11.520
there be no money in my pocket

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:13.603
and understanding that
feeling of being hungry.

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:16.923
Not knowing if I'm going
to get something to eat

00:24:18.020 --> 00:24:21.537
Not knowing where I'm going
to get something to eat at.

00:24:21.537 --> 00:24:23.403
Not even having a cup of water.

00:24:26.580 --> 00:24:27.490
I mean, wake ups

00:24:29.290 --> 00:24:32.180
Already off the ground, just
sleeping on the sidewalk.

00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:33.780
The body already sore

00:24:35.270 --> 00:24:37.550
from the ground causing
so much pain in your back

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:38.847
and in your body.

00:24:40.630 --> 00:24:43.513
So you're starting off with
getting up off the ground.

00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:50.690
And whatever little stuff that
you had laying around you,

00:24:50.690 --> 00:24:51.680
it's already gone

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:53.530
they took it or been rambled through.

00:24:54.950 --> 00:24:56.300
So you're dealing with that

00:24:58.890 --> 00:25:00.980
And you'd have been on some
of the same blocks already

00:25:00.980 --> 00:25:05.370
that you didn't already ask the
same people to help you out.

00:25:05.370 --> 00:25:08.653
So you don't want to keep
burning your bridges on that.

00:25:10.140 --> 00:25:12.640
So now you're thinking of a plan like, man

00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:15.060
I'm going to go to a store or something

00:25:15.060 --> 00:25:17.630
walk around that store and
just get something to eat.

00:25:17.630 --> 00:25:18.573
Without any money,

00:25:20.070 --> 00:25:20.903
you're hungry

00:25:22.990 --> 00:25:24.820
And I had done that.

00:25:24.820 --> 00:25:26.970
I'd go to Ralph's or Target or something.

00:25:26.970 --> 00:25:29.010
I would just start opening
up food and walking around

00:25:29.010 --> 00:25:31.822
like I'm shopping, but I'm
eating because I'm hungry.

00:25:31.822 --> 00:25:32.655
I don't have any money

00:25:33.530 --> 00:25:34.880
so I can get through today.

00:25:38.562 --> 00:25:40.473
You know, going in the bathroom in there.

00:25:41.358 --> 00:25:44.340
And just wash my face and wash up.

00:25:44.340 --> 00:25:45.390
Clean up a little bit

00:25:46.930 --> 00:25:49.240
so that no one noticed that I, you know

00:25:49.240 --> 00:25:52.453
slept outside or anything like that.

00:25:55.995 --> 00:25:58.860
And then hoping that the day would change

00:25:58.860 --> 00:26:00.250
throughout that.

00:26:00.250 --> 00:26:01.650
Hoping that somewhere or someway

00:26:01.650 --> 00:26:04.930
or somehow I'll find some
luck to get some money

00:26:04.930 --> 00:26:06.013
because now I ate.

00:26:07.222 --> 00:26:08.055
And I had something to drink

00:26:08.055 --> 00:26:09.070
and I'm washed up a little bit.

00:26:09.070 --> 00:26:10.880
Now I'm going to get high.

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:12.730
So now, you know, I'm plotting on how

00:26:14.250 --> 00:26:15.600
I'm gonna get my next high.

00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:20.033
And I come on and we try
to come on with that plan.

00:26:21.010 --> 00:26:23.956
So I would stay walking around
and my feet start hurting

00:26:23.956 --> 00:26:26.430
and I would sit down
and I'm already tired.

00:26:26.430 --> 00:26:27.960
I'll eat something and I'll fall asleep,

00:26:27.960 --> 00:26:30.743
right where I'm at unintentionally.

00:26:32.147 --> 00:26:34.930
But my body would be so tired
to where I would fall asleep

00:26:36.570 --> 00:26:38.691
and wake up and stuff gone.

00:26:38.691 --> 00:26:41.091
And sometimes I wake up,
my stuff's still there.

00:26:45.217 --> 00:26:46.590
It's like, everybody's
going to get that chance

00:26:46.590 --> 00:26:48.890
to where you're going
to deal with so much.

00:26:48.890 --> 00:26:50.440
It's like your turn, your turn.

00:26:52.200 --> 00:26:54.070
I mean, I didn't have days where it work

00:26:54.070 --> 00:26:55.943
oh, the whole day was real bad.

00:26:57.410 --> 00:26:58.700
It was no luck happening,

00:26:58.700 --> 00:27:00.337
was nothing going on.

00:27:00.337 --> 00:27:01.610
It just seemed like man life is over

00:27:05.820 --> 00:27:06.653
Downtown.

00:27:10.330 --> 00:27:12.730
You really meet the heart
of a person down here.

00:27:16.166 --> 00:27:19.916
You really get a chance
to find out the good,

00:27:21.511 --> 00:27:23.599
the bad, the indifferent.

00:27:23.599 --> 00:27:24.516
Right here.

00:27:25.922 --> 00:27:27.172
You can see it.

